@startuml
title Zenval — Bounded contexts
caption PROPOSED TARGET — chưa phải implementation / scope MVP đã duyệt
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam nodesep 55
skinparam ranksep 90
hide empty methods
left to right direction
package "Identity & Access" as IAM {}
package Ledger as L {}
package "Classification & Capture" as C {}
package "Commitments & Planning" as P {}
package Obligations as O {}
package Investments as I {}
package Goals as G {}
package "Market Data" as M {}
package Reporting as R {}
package Suggestions as S {}
package Notifications as N {}
package "Audit & Compliance" as A {}
L ..> IAM : authorization port
C ..> L : posting application port
O ..> L : posting application port
I ..> L : cash posting application port
I ..> M : price / FX query port
L ..> M : FX reference port
G ..> L : account projection
G ..> I : holding projection
P ..> L : facts query port
P ..> O : schedules query port
P ..> G : allocation query port
S ..> P : read snapshots / create draft
R ..> L : read projections
R ..> O : read projections
R ..> I : read projections
R ..> G : read projections
R ..> P : read projections
N ..> P : consume integration events
N ..> O : consume integration events
A ..> L : consume audit events
A ..> P : consume audit events
note bottom of A
  Audit subscriptions apply across all contexts.
  Export/delete use explicit application ports.
end note
legend bottom
  A ..> B = A consumes B through a port/contract/event.
  No direct cross-context domain/table access.
  Source: ARCHITECTURE §§5–6; not deployment topology.
endlegend
@enduml
